"use strict";(self.webpackChunkwoocommerce_multivendor_marketplace_docs=self.webpackChunkwoocommerce_multivendor_marketplace_docs||[]).push([[8311],{12535(e,t,n){e.exports=n.p+"assets/img/product-list.3afe5d34.webp"},77839(e,t,n){n.r(t),n.d(t,{comp:()=>k,data:()=>w});var a=n(20641);const i=n.p+"assets/img/Product-mangement.e7b4a764.webp",r=n.p+"assets/img/productlist-1.7f32a1d6.webp",s=n.p+"assets/img/admin-marketplace-products-table-live.63fa5dc8.png",o=n.p+"assets/img/filter-by-vendor.646388b7.webp",l=n.p+"assets/img/admin-marketplace-filter-assign-bar.60f2525c.png",d=n.p+"assets/img/admin-marketplace-products-filtered-vendor.d08fa05a.png",c=n.p+"assets/img/assign-vendor.7a1c1884.webp",p=n.p+"assets/img/admin-marketplace-assign-vendor-live.0d80af9e.png",g=n.p+"assets/img/allow-seller-woocommerce-marketplace.14f13381.webp",u=n.p+"assets/img/Productlist-3.99f37e88.webp";var m=n(12535);const h=n.p+"assets/img/admin-product-edit-page-overview.29090970.png",f=n.p+"assets/img/admin-product-edit-vendor-metabox.ce54af21.png",b=n.p+"assets/img/admin-product-edit-max-qty-setting.9da51552.png",v={class:"hint-container note"},y={},k=(0,n(66262).A)(y,[["render",function(e,t){const n=(0,a.g2)("RouteLink");return(0,a.uX)(),(0,a.CE)("div",null,[t[8]||(t[8]=(0,a.Fv)('<h1 id="marketplace-product-management" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#marketplace-product-management"><span>Marketplace Product Management</span></a></h1><p>After installing the <strong>WooCommerce Marketplace plugin</strong>, store administrators can easily manage all marketplace products from WordPress admin to maintain complete control over multi-vendor inventory.</p><p>From the <strong>Marketplace → Products</strong> console, admins can review vendor submissions, filter items by seller, approve new drafts, mass-assign catalog items, and set custom order purchase limits for shoppers.</p><div class="hint-container tip"><p class="hint-container-title">Centralized Catalog Control</p><p>The <strong>Marketplace Products</strong> console gives the store administrator complete visibility over the entire multi-vendor catalog. Store owners can oversee vendor inventory, approve or reject new product submissions, assign unallocated products to specific vendors, and enforce marketplace purchasing policies.</p></div><p><a class="doc-image-link" href="./assets/Product-mangement.webp"><img src="'+i+'" alt="Product List – All Products"></a></p><hr><h2 id="marketplace-overview" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#marketplace-overview"><span>Marketplace Overview</span></a></h2><p>From the admin panel, the admin can manage:</p><ul><li>Vendors</li><li>Products</li><li>Commissions</li><li>Marketplace settings (such as product auto-publish and vendor auto-approval)</li></ul><hr><h2 id="product-management-by-admin" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#product-management-by-admin"><span>Product Management by Admin</span></a></h2><ul><li>The admin can create and publish all types of products: <ul><li>Simple</li><li>Virtual</li><li>Downloadable</li><li>Grouped</li><li>External / Affiliate</li><li>Variable</li></ul></li><li>Products can be assigned to one or more vendors.</li><li>The admin has full control over vendor-created products.</li></ul><hr><h2 id="product-list-admin-end" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#product-list-admin-end"><span>Product List (Admin End)</span></a></h2><p>In the <strong>Product List</strong>, the admin can:</p><ul><li>View both <strong>admin</strong> and <strong>vendor</strong> products</li><li>Edit or delete any product</li><li>Modify any product specification created by vendors</li><li>Filter products by vendor</li><li>Mass-assign products to vendors</li><li><strong>Screen Options</strong>: Admins can easily show or hide specific columns on the admin Products listing page using the standard Screen Options menu to customize their view.</li></ul><p><a class="doc-image-link" href="./assets/productlist-1.webp"><img src="'+r+'" alt="Product List – All Products"></a></p><h3 id="marketplace-products-management-console" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#marketplace-products-management-console"><span>Marketplace Products Management Console</span></a></h3><p>Admins access the product catalog from <strong>WordPress Admin → Marketplace → Products</strong>.</p><p><a class="doc-image-link" href="./assets/admin-marketplace-products-table-live.png"><img src="'+s+'" alt="Marketplace Products Central Management Table"></a></p><h3 id="table-columns-breakdown" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#table-columns-breakdown"><span>Table Columns Breakdown</span></a></h3><p>The Marketplace Products table displays key catalog and vendor details across 12 structured columns:</p><table><thead><tr><th style="text-align:left;">Column Header</th><th style="text-align:left;">Field Type</th><th style="text-align:left;">Description</th><th style="text-align:left;">Available Actions</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td style="text-align:left;"><strong>Checkbox</strong></td><td style="text-align:left;">Bulk Selector</td><td style="text-align:left;">Checkbox to select single or multiple products.</td><td style="text-align:left;">Apply bulk trash actions or mass-assign products to a vendor.</td></tr><tr><td style="text-align:left;"><strong>Image</strong></td><td style="text-align:left;">Thumbnail</td><td style="text-align:left;">Visual preview of the product&#39;s primary featured image.</td><td style="text-align:left;">Quick visual verification of product image assets.</td></tr><tr><td style="text-align:left;"><strong>Product</strong></td><td style="text-align:left;">Title &amp; Actions</td><td style="text-align:left;">Product title (sortable ascending/descending).</td><td style="text-align:left;">Hover to display inline quick links: <strong>Edit</strong> (opens the WooCommerce product editor) and <strong>View</strong> (opens the storefront product page).</td></tr><tr><td style="text-align:left;"><strong>SKU</strong></td><td style="text-align:left;">Unique Code</td><td style="text-align:left;">Stock Keeping Unit identifier defined for the product.</td><td style="text-align:left;">Simplifies warehouse and stock tracking across vendors.</td></tr><tr><td style="text-align:left;"><strong>Stock</strong></td><td style="text-align:left;">Inventory Status</td><td style="text-align:left;">Current stock condition (e.g., <code>Instock</code>, <code>Out of stock</code>, or remaining inventory count).</td><td style="text-align:left;">Highlights stock availability in real time.</td></tr><tr><td style="text-align:left;"><strong>Price</strong></td><td style="text-align:left;">Currency Amount</td><td style="text-align:left;">Regular and sale price, or price range for variable items.</td><td style="text-align:left;">Sortable ascending/descending to monitor product price ranges.</td></tr><tr><td style="text-align:left;"><strong>Flags</strong></td><td style="text-align:left;">Numeric Counter</td><td style="text-align:left;">Total count of customer reports or flags submitted against this item.</td><td style="text-align:left;">Alerts admin to review products flagged by marketplace shoppers.</td></tr><tr><td style="text-align:left;"><strong>Categories</strong></td><td style="text-align:left;">Taxonomy List</td><td style="text-align:left;">WooCommerce product categories assigned to the item.</td><td style="text-align:left;">Helps organize and categorize vendor items on the store.</td></tr><tr><td style="text-align:left;"><strong>Tags</strong></td><td style="text-align:left;">Taxonomy List</td><td style="text-align:left;">Keywords and product tags associated with the product.</td><td style="text-align:left;">Enhances storefront search and filtering.</td></tr><tr><td style="text-align:left;"><strong>Featured</strong></td><td style="text-align:left;">Boolean Status</td><td style="text-align:left;">Indicates whether the product is highlighted as a featured listing (<code>Yes</code> or <code>No</code>).</td><td style="text-align:left;">Quickly identify top promoted catalog items.</td></tr><tr><td style="text-align:left;"><strong>Type</strong></td><td style="text-align:left;">Product Type</td><td style="text-align:left;">WooCommerce product type (e.g., <code>Simple</code>, <code>Variable</code>, <code>Grouped</code>, <code>External</code>).</td><td style="text-align:left;">Clarifies product architecture and data format.</td></tr><tr><td style="text-align:left;"><strong>Date</strong></td><td style="text-align:left;">Date &amp; Status</td><td style="text-align:left;">Creation timestamp and publication status (e.g., <code>August 15, 2026 | Publish</code> or <code>October 12, 2026 | Draft</code>).</td><td style="text-align:left;">Sortable ascending/descending; immediately identifies newly submitted drafts.</td></tr><tr><td style="text-align:left;"><strong>Vendor</strong></td><td style="text-align:left;">Vendor Name</td><td style="text-align:left;">Business name of the seller assigned to the product (or <code>Demo Admin</code>).</td><td style="text-align:left;">Identifies who owns the item and receives order revenue.</td></tr></tbody></table><h3 id="search-products-functionality" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#search-products-functionality"><span>Search Products Functionality</span></a></h3><p>The dedicated search bar at the top right of the table allows admins to find products quickly:</p><ul><li>Enter product titles, partial names, or SKU codes into the <strong>Search Products</strong> field.</li><li>Click the <strong>Search Products</strong> button to display matching results instantly across all vendor listings.</li></ul><h3 id="bulk-actions-move-to-trash" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#bulk-actions-move-to-trash"><span>Bulk Actions (Move to Trash)</span></a></h3><ul><li>Mark the checkboxes next to any products you wish to remove.</li><li>Select <strong>Trash</strong> from the <strong>Bulk actions</strong> dropdown menu.</li><li>Click <strong>Apply</strong> to move all selected products to the trash.</li></ul><h3 id="screen-options-customization" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#screen-options-customization"><span>Screen Options Customization</span></a></h3><p>Admins can customize which columns appear in the table by opening the <strong>Screen Options</strong> panel at the top right:</p><ul><li>Toggle checkboxes for any column: <em>Image, Product, SKU, Stock, Price, Flags, Categories, Tags, Featured, Type, Date, Vendor</em>.</li><li>Set the <strong>Number of items per page</strong> (pagination limit) to manage how many products appear per page.</li><li>Click <strong>Apply</strong> to save your preferred view.</li></ul><hr><h2 id="filter-products-by-vendor" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#filter-products-by-vendor"><span>Filter Products by Vendor</span></a></h2><ul><li>Admin can filter the product list based on a specific vendor.</li><li>Once filtered, only the selected vendor’s products will be displayed.</li></ul><p><a class="doc-image-link" href="./assets/filter-by-vendor.webp"><img src="'+o+'" alt="Product List – Vendor Filtered"></a></p><h3 id="dual-filter-controls-vendor-assignment-status" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#dual-filter-controls-vendor-assignment-status"><span>Dual Filter Controls (Vendor &amp; Assignment Status)</span></a></h3><p>The filter toolbar above the table provides two targeted filtering dimensions to help manage marketplace inventory:</p><p><a class="doc-image-link" href="./assets/admin-marketplace-filter-assign-bar.png"><img src="'+l+'" alt="Filter and Assign Controls Bar"></a></p><ol><li><p><strong>Filter by Vendor</strong>:</p><ul><li>Select a specific registered seller from the <strong>Filter by Vendor</strong> dropdown menu (e.g., <em>Aurora Athletics</em>, <em>Volt &amp; Vine</em>, <em>Copperleaf Kitchen</em>).</li><li>Shows only products owned by that vendor.</li></ul></li><li><p><strong>Filter by Assignment Status</strong>:</p><ul><li><strong>Assigned</strong>: Displays products that are currently linked to an active marketplace vendor.</li><li><strong>UnAssigned</strong>: Displays standalone or orphaned products that do not have an assigned vendor yet.</li></ul></li><li><p>Click the <strong>Filter</strong> button to apply the selected filter criteria.</p></li></ol><p><a class="doc-image-link" href="./assets/admin-marketplace-products-filtered-vendor.png"><img src="'+d+'" alt="Filtered Vendor Products View"></a></p><div class="hint-container info"><p class="hint-container-title">Why the UnAssigned Filter Is Useful</p><p>When a store admin imports bulk products into WooCommerce or creates catalog products before onboarding sellers, those products remain unassigned. Filtering by <strong>UnAssigned</strong> instantly displays all products waiting to be allocated to vendors.</p></div><hr><h2 id="assign-products-to-vendor" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#assign-products-to-vendor"><span>Assign Products to Vendor</span></a></h2><ul><li>Select: <ul><li>One or more products</li><li>A vendor from the dropdown</li></ul></li><li>Click the <strong>Assign</strong> button to assign selected products to the chosen vendor.</li></ul><p><a class="doc-image-link" href="./assets/assign-vendor.webp"><img src="'+c+'" alt="Assign Products to Vendor"></a></p><h3 id="step-by-step-mass-vendor-assignment" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#step-by-step-mass-vendor-assignment"><span>Step-by-Step Mass Vendor Assignment</span></a></h3><p>Store admins can reassign or allocate products in bulk directly from the Marketplace Products list:</p><p><a class="doc-image-link" href="./assets/admin-marketplace-assign-vendor-live.png"><img src="'+p+'" alt="Assign Products to Vendor Toolbar in Action"></a></p><ol><li><strong>Select Products</strong>: Mark the checkboxes next to the products you want to assign (or click the header checkbox to select all visible products).</li><li><strong>Choose Vendor</strong>: In the toolbar, click the <strong>Select Vendor</strong> dropdown menu and choose the target vendor.</li><li><strong>Execute Assignment</strong>: Click the <strong>Assign</strong> button.</li><li><strong>Instant Confirmation</strong>: The page refreshes with an update notification, and the <strong>Vendor</strong> column immediately reflects the new seller assignment for all selected products.</li></ol><hr><h2 id="vendor-product-approval-manual-publish" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#vendor-product-approval-manual-publish"><span>Vendor Product Approval (Manual Publish)</span></a></h2><p>If the admin has configured <strong>Allow Vendor to Publish</strong> as <strong>unchecked</strong>:</p><ul><li>Vendor-added products will be created in <strong>Draft</strong> status.</li><li>Admin must manually review and publish the product.</li></ul><p><a class="doc-image-link" href="./assets/allow-seller-woocommerce-marketplace.webp"><img src="'+g+'" alt="Allow Vendor to Publish Setting"></a></p>',54)),(0,a.Lk)("div",v,[t[7]||(t[7]=(0,a.Lk)("p",{class:"hint-container-title"},"Setting Configuration Location",-1)),(0,a.Lk)("p",null,[t[1]||(t[1]=(0,a.eW)("To enforce manual product approval, navigate to ")),t[2]||(t[2]=(0,a.Lk)("strong",null,"Marketplace → Settings → General Settings",-1)),t[3]||(t[3]=(0,a.eW)(" and ensure ")),t[4]||(t[4]=(0,a.Lk)("strong",null,"Allow Vendor to Publish",-1)),t[5]||(t[5]=(0,a.eW)(" is unchecked. For more details on global marketplace switches, see the ")),(0,a.bF)(n,{to:"/documentation/configuration-general-settings.html"},{default:(0,a.k6)(()=>t[0]||(t[0]=[(0,a.eW)("General Configuration Guide")])),_:1}),t[6]||(t[6]=(0,a.eW)("."))])]),t[9]||(t[9]=(0,a.Fv)('<hr><h2 id="draft-product-visibility" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#draft-product-visibility"><span>Draft Product Visibility</span></a></h2><ul><li>When a vendor adds a product: <ul><li>Product status remains <strong>Draft</strong></li><li>Product is visible in the admin product list</li></ul></li></ul><p><a class="doc-image-link" href="./assets/Productlist-3.webp"><img src="'+u+'" alt="Draft Product in Admin List"></a></p><p>In the Marketplace Products list table, draft products clearly indicate their pending status in the <strong>Date</strong> column (e.g., <code>October 12, 2026 | Draft</code>), allowing administrators to quickly spot submissions requiring review.</p><hr><h2 id="publish-vendor-product" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#publish-vendor-product"><span>Publish Vendor Product</span></a></h2><ul><li>Admin edits the draft product.</li><li>Clicks the <strong>Publish</strong> button.</li><li>Product becomes live on the storefront.</li></ul><p><a class="doc-image-link" href="./assets/product-list.webp"><img src="'+m+'" alt="Publish Vendor Product"></a></p><h3 id="admin-review-publishing-checklist" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#admin-review-publishing-checklist"><span>Admin Review &amp; Publishing Checklist</span></a></h3><p>Before publishing vendor products, administrators typically verify:</p><ol><li>Accurate product title, category, and tags.</li><li>Reasonable pricing and inventory counts.</li><li>High-quality product images compliant with marketplace guidelines.</li><li>Correct vendor attribution in the <strong>Vendor</strong> meta box.</li></ol><hr><h2 id="editing-marketplace-products-admin-edit-screen" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#editing-marketplace-products-admin-edit-screen"><span>Editing Marketplace Products (Admin Edit Screen)</span></a></h2><p>When an administrator clicks <strong>Edit</strong> on any product in the Marketplace Products list or from the standard WooCommerce product catalog, the product editing interface opens.</p><p><a class="doc-image-link" href="./assets/admin-product-edit-page-overview.png"><img src="'+h+'" alt="Admin Edit Product Page Overview"></a></p><div class="hint-container tip"><p class="hint-container-title">Standard WooCommerce Product Fields</p><p>Creating and configuring standard product fields—such as <strong>Product Title, Long Description, Short Description, Categories, Tags, Featured Image, Product Gallery, Pricing, Tax, Shipping Dimensions, Linked Products (Upsells/Cross-sells), Attributes, and Variations</strong>—is handled by core WooCommerce.</p><p>For step-by-step guidance on standard WooCommerce product setup, refer to the official WooCommerce documentation:</p><ul><li><a href="https://woocommerce.com/document/managing-products/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Adding and Managing Products (WooCommerce Official Guide)</a></li><li><a href="https://woocommerce.com/document/managing-product-categories-tags-attributes/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Managing Product Categories, Tags, and Attributes</a></li><li><a href="https://woocommerce.com/document/variable-product/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Variable Products Setup &amp; Variations</a></li></ul></div><h3 id="vendor-specific-fields-in-the-edit-screen" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#vendor-specific-fields-in-the-edit-screen"><span>Vendor-Specific Fields in the Edit Screen</span></a></h3><p>The WooCommerce Marketplace plugin introduces dedicated marketplace fields on the edit screen to connect products with vendors and control buyer purchasing rules:</p><h4 id="_1-vendor-assignment-panel" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#_1-vendor-assignment-panel"><span>1. Vendor Assignment Panel</span></a></h4><p>Located in the right sidebar (or main editing area), the <strong>Vendor</strong> panel controls vendor ownership for the product:</p><p><a class="doc-image-link" href="./assets/admin-product-edit-vendor-metabox.png"><img src="'+f+'" alt="Vendor Meta Box on Edit Product Page"></a></p><ul><li><strong>Vendor Dropdown</strong>: Select the seller who owns the product. The list includes all registered marketplace sellers as well as the store administrator (<code>Demo Admin</code>).</li><li><strong>Transferring Ownership</strong>: Changing the vendor and clicking <strong>Update</strong> instantly transfers ownership of the product. The product will now appear in the new vendor&#39;s dashboard and profile catalog.</li><li><strong>Order Attribution &amp; Commissions</strong>: When an order is placed for this product, commission calculations and order revenue will automatically route to the vendor assigned in this box.</li></ul><h4 id="_2-maximum-purchasable-quantity-limit" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#_2-maximum-purchasable-quantity-limit"><span>2. Maximum Purchasable Quantity Limit</span></a></h4><p>Located inside the WooCommerce <strong>Product Data</strong> panel under the <strong>Inventory</strong> tab:</p><p><a class="doc-image-link" href="./assets/admin-product-edit-max-qty-setting.png"><img src="'+b+'" alt="Maximum Purchasable Quantity in Product Data Inventory"></a></p><ul><li><strong>Field</strong>: <strong>Maximum Purchasable Quantity</strong></li><li><strong>Purpose</strong>: Restricts how many units of this vendor&#39;s product a customer can purchase in a single order.</li><li><strong>Usage</strong>: <ul><li>Enter a whole number (e.g., <code>5</code>) to prevent bulk purchasing, hoarding, or stock exhaustion on limited-edition vendor items.</li><li>Leave blank to allow customers to purchase up to the standard stock availability.</li></ul></li><li>Click <strong>Update</strong> to save the quantity limit.</li></ul><hr><h2 id="frontend-visibility" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#frontend-visibility"><span>Frontend Visibility</span></a></h2><ul><li>Once published, the product is: <ul><li>Visible to customers on the frontend</li><li>Available for purchase like any other WooCommerce product</li></ul></li></ul><p>On the storefront single product page, the marketplace displays the assigned vendor&#39;s details:</p><ul><li><strong>Sold By / Vendor Name</strong>: Displays a clickable link to the vendor&#39;s profile shop.</li><li><strong>Vendor Badges</strong>: Verified achievement badges assigned to the seller appear alongside vendor details.</li><li><strong>Ask a Question</strong>: Shoppers can inquire about the product directly with the vendor if enabled.</li></ul><hr><h2 id="key-benefits" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#key-benefits"><span>Key Benefits</span></a></h2><ul><li><strong>Full administrative control</strong> over marketplace products and vendor submissions</li><li><strong>Secure approval workflow</strong> preventing unverified products from going live automatically</li><li><strong>Dual filtering capabilities</strong> by specific vendor and assigned/unassigned status</li><li><strong>Rapid mass-assignment tool</strong> to allocate multiple products to sellers with one click</li><li><strong>Granular purchase limits</strong> via Maximum Purchasable Quantity protection</li><li><strong>Centralized product management</strong> designed to scale with growing multi-vendor marketplaces</li></ul><hr><h2 id="related-guides" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#related-guides"><span>Related Guides</span></a></h2><ul><li><a href="/documentation/admin-select-and-sell" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">MP Select and Sell</a> – Manage multi-seller single product catalog listings, Global eligibility, and vendor offers.</li><li><a href="/documentation/selling-existing-products" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Selling Existing Products</a> – Vendor-facing guide for attaching competing offers to existing catalog items.</li><li><a href="/documentation/vendor-mangement" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Vendor Badges</a> – Reward top-performing merchants with trust badges displayed across catalog pages.</li><li><a href="/documentation/admin-staff-setting" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Admin Staff Settings</a> – Delegate product management and Select &amp; Sell capabilities to vendor staff.</li></ul>',38))])}]]),w=JSON.parse('{"path":"/documentation/admin-panel-management.html","title":"Marketplace Product Management","lang":"en-US","frontmatter":{"title":"Marketplace Product Management","description":"Complete administrator guide for managing marketplace products, filtering by vendor, mass assigning products, manual approval workflows, and vendor-specific product settings in WooCommerce Multi-Vendor Marketplace.","head":[["meta",{"name":"keywords","content":"woocommerce marketplace product management, assign product to vendor woocommerce, filter products by vendor, marketplace products admin panel, manual product approval, vendor metabox woocommerce, maximum purchasable quantity marketplace"}],["meta",{"property":"og:title","content":"Marketplace Product Management | WooCommerce Multi-Vendor Marketplace"}],["meta",{"property":"og:description","content":"Complete administrator guide for managing marketplace products, filtering by vendor, mass assigning products, manual approval workflows, and vendor-specific product settings in WooCommerce Multi-Vendor Marketplace."}],["meta",{"property":"og:type","content":"article"}]]},"headers":[{"level":2,"title":"Marketplace Overview","slug":"marketplace-overview","link":"#marketplace-overview","children":[]},{"level":2,"title":"Product Management by Admin","slug":"product-management-by-admin","link":"#product-management-by-admin","children":[]},{"level":2,"title":"Product List (Admin End)","slug":"product-list-admin-end","link":"#product-list-admin-end","children":[{"level":3,"title":"Marketplace Products Management Console","slug":"marketplace-products-management-console","link":"#marketplace-products-management-console","children":[]},{"level":3,"title":"Table Columns Breakdown","slug":"table-columns-breakdown","link":"#table-columns-breakdown","children":[]},{"level":3,"title":"Search Products Functionality","slug":"search-products-functionality","link":"#search-products-functionality","children":[]},{"level":3,"title":"Bulk Actions (Move to Trash)","slug":"bulk-actions-move-to-trash","link":"#bulk-actions-move-to-trash","children":[]},{"level":3,"title":"Screen Options Customization","slug":"screen-options-customization","link":"#screen-options-customization","children":[]}]},{"level":2,"title":"Filter Products by Vendor","slug":"filter-products-by-vendor","link":"#filter-products-by-vendor","children":[{"level":3,"title":"Dual Filter Controls (Vendor & Assignment Status)","slug":"dual-filter-controls-vendor-assignment-status","link":"#dual-filter-controls-vendor-assignment-status","children":[]}]},{"level":2,"title":"Assign Products to Vendor","slug":"assign-products-to-vendor","link":"#assign-products-to-vendor","children":[{"level":3,"title":"Step-by-Step Mass Vendor Assignment","slug":"step-by-step-mass-vendor-assignment","link":"#step-by-step-mass-vendor-assignment","children":[]}]},{"level":2,"title":"Vendor Product Approval (Manual Publish)","slug":"vendor-product-approval-manual-publish","link":"#vendor-product-approval-manual-publish","children":[]},{"level":2,"title":"Draft Product Visibility","slug":"draft-product-visibility","link":"#draft-product-visibility","children":[]},{"level":2,"title":"Publish Vendor Product","slug":"publish-vendor-product","link":"#publish-vendor-product","children":[{"level":3,"title":"Admin Review & Publishing Checklist","slug":"admin-review-publishing-checklist","link":"#admin-review-publishing-checklist","children":[]}]},{"level":2,"title":"Editing Marketplace Products (Admin Edit Screen)","slug":"editing-marketplace-products-admin-edit-screen","link":"#editing-marketplace-products-admin-edit-screen","children":[{"level":3,"title":"Vendor-Specific Fields in the Edit Screen","slug":"vendor-specific-fields-in-the-edit-screen","link":"#vendor-specific-fields-in-the-edit-screen","children":[]}]},{"level":2,"title":"Frontend Visibility","slug":"frontend-visibility","link":"#frontend-visibility","children":[]},{"level":2,"title":"Key Benefits","slug":"key-benefits","link":"#key-benefits","children":[]},{"level":2,"title":"Related Guides","slug":"related-guides","link":"#related-guides","children":[]}],"git":{},"filePathRelative":"documentation/admin-panel-management.md"}')}}]);